
# To add viswa to sudoers list
============================
Better practice: use /etc/sudoers.d/
Instead of editing /etc/sudoers directly, it's recommended to create a separate file:

echo "viswa ALL=(ALL) ALL" | sudo tee /etc/sudoers.d/viswa
sudo chmod 440 /etc/sudoers.d/viswa



# verify the configuration
==========================

sudo visudo -c

# Expected output:
/etc/sudoers: parsed OK
/etc/sudoers.d/viswa: parsed OK









To remove sudo access later, simply delete the file:
===================================================
sudo rm /etc/sudoers.d/viswa

This approach is safer and easier to manage than modifying the main /etc/sudoers file.


