Create one file containing multiple users
=========================================

# Create a single file:
sudo vi /etc/sudoers.d/devops-users

# Add:
viswa ALL=(ALL) ALL
john  ALL=(ALL) ALL
alice ALL=(ALL) ALL

# Set permissions:
sudo chmod 440 /etc/sudoers.d/devops-users

# Verify the configuration
sudo visudo -c

# Expected output:
/etc/sudoers: parsed OK
/etc/sudoers.d/viswa: parsed OK
/etc/sudoers.d/john: parsed OK
/etc/sudoers.d/alice: parsed OK

# or, if using a single file:
/etc/sudoers.d/devops-users: parsed OK









To remove one user's access later, edit the file and delete that user's line.
============================================================================

sudo vi /etc/sudoers.d/devops-users


remove:
=======
john  ALL=(ALL) ALL


# Set permissions:
sudo chmod 440 /etc/sudoers.d/devops-users

# Verify the configuration
sudo visudo -c

# Expected output:
/etc/sudoers: parsed OK
/etc/sudoers.d/viswa: parsed OK
/etc/sudoers.d/alice: parsed OK

# or, if using a single file:
/etc/sudoers.d/devops-users: parsed OK









